-- title:
--   Rescaled-logarithm Witt vectors lie in `wittHom` and `fontaineKer`
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $\mathcal O$ a commutative ring in which $p$ is a non-zero-divisor, equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure on $\mathbb Z/p$ whose structure map has kernel $(p)$, and which is adically complete for $(p)$. Let $F$ be a $d$-dimensional commutative formal group law over $\mathcal O$ (a $d$-tuple of power series in the variables $\mathrm{inl}\,j,\mathrm{inr}\,j$, with zero constant term, linear part $X_i+Y_i$, associative, and symmetric under swapping the two blocks). Let $F_p$ be a $d$-tuple of power series in $2d$ variables with zero constant coefficients satisfying $\mathrm{coeff}_m(F_p{}_i)\cdot p=p^{|m|}\,\mathrm{coeff}_m(F_i)$ for all $m\neq 0$, and let $\varphi=(\varphi_i)$ be $d$ power series in $X_1,\dots,X_d$ with zero constant coefficients, linear part the identity matrix, coefficients tending to $0$ $p$-adically (for every $N$, all but finitely many coefficients lie in $(p^N)$), and satisfying $\varphi_i\circ F_p=\varphi_i(\mathrm{inl})+\varphi_i(\mathrm{inr})$. Let $v\in\mathbb N$ and let $R$ be a Hopf algebra over $\mathcal O$, free and finite as an $\mathcal O$-module, with $R$ and $R\otimes_{\mathcal O}R$ adically complete for the ideal generated by $p$. Let $\pi:\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]\to R$ be a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map such that each $\pi(X_i)$ lies in the radical of $(p)\subseteq R$, such that $\pi$ is given on every power series by adic evaluation at the points $\pi(X_i)$, such that $\ker\pi$ is the ideal generated by the components of $F$'s $p^v$-th iterate series `F.nthSeries (p ^ v)` (defined by $[\,0\,]=0$ and $[\,n+1\,]_i=F_i([\,n\,],X)$), and such that the comultiplication of $R$ sends $\pi(X_i)$ to the adic evaluation of $F_i$ at $(\pi(X_j)\otimes 1,\,1\otimes\pi(X_j))$; assume finally that the Cartier dual of $\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}R$, i.e. its $\mathbb Z/p$-linear dual, is a local ring. The conclusion is that there is $N_0$ such that for every $N\ge N_0$ and every $i$ there exists a Witt vector $\ell\in W(\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_d]])$ with: for each exponent $m$, if $|m|\le N$ then $\mathrm{coeff}_m$ of the $(N-1)$-st ghost component of $\ell$ equals $p^{\,N-|m|}\mathrm{coeff}_m(\varphi_i)$, while if $|m|>N$ then either $\mathrm{coeff}_m(\mathrm{ghost}_{N-1}\ell)\cdot p^{\,|m|-N}=\mathrm{coeff}_m(\varphi_i)$ or $\mathrm{coeff}_m(\mathrm{ghost}_{N-1}\ell)=0$ and $p^{\,|m|-N}\nmid\mathrm{coeff}_m(\varphi_i)$; and, writing $\iota$ for $R\to\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}R$, $r\mapsto 1\otimes r$, the length-$N$ truncation of $W(\iota\circ\pi)(\ell)$ both satisfies the additivity condition defining [`Deformation.wittHom`](def/Dieudonne_WittVectorHom.html#L246), namely that applying $W_N$ of the comultiplication of $\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}R$ to it gives the sum of its images under $W_N$ of the two inclusions into the tensor square, and lies in [`Deformation.TruncWitt.fontaineKer p N`](def/Dieudonne_FontaineHodge.html#L76) for $\iota$, i.e. it is the truncation of $W(\iota)(X)$ for some $X\in W(R)$ whose $(N-1)$-st ghost component lies in $(p^N)\subseteq R$.
--
--   This is the construction step that turns the integral rescaled logarithm of a commutative formal group law into elements of the Dieudonné module of the $p^v$-torsion in Fontaine's Witt-covector description: the truncated Witt vector produced is a homomorphism-type (additive) element of `wittHom` lying in the kernel of the relevant ghost map. It is used by [`Deformation.exists_algHom_baseChange_eq_of_forall_map_mem_fontaineKer_of_mvFormalGroup`](thm.html#Deformation.exists_algHom_baseChange_eq_of_forall_map_mem_fontaineKer_of_mvFormalGroup), and it cites the integrality of the logarithm coefficients, the existence of the Witt vector with prescribed ghost components, and the two preceding statements about the truncated image and the ghost congruence.
-- source:
